{
  "id": "cantigas_de_santa_maria",
  "name": "Cantigas de Santa María (Alfonsine Marian songs)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "The Cantigas de Santa María are some 420 Marian songs in Galician-Portuguese compiled at the court of Alfonso X of Castile in the 1270s and 1280s and preserved in four manuscripts now held at El Escorial, Madrid and Florence, three of them with musical notation; the miniatures of the Escorial códice de los músicos show players of fiddles, lutes, psalteries, hurdy-gurdies, shawms, bagpipes and drums. The notation gives a single melodic line, so modern early-music ensembles reconstruct rhythm, drones and instrumentation, and the corpus has become one of the most recorded bodies of medieval song. The oud card stands for the lute shown in the miniatures.",
  "recipe": "classic European mid-1270s cantigas de santa maría, art Music, western early branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, pure fifth stacked, single lead single track no stacking. vielle medieval, oud, medieval psaltery, credited frame drums. parish church. blumlein stereo pair, ultra-clean solid-state pre. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
